    summary: "Many in the city are doubling down on making products aimed at wealthier customers overseas despite the emergence of trade barriers.",
    preview: "SHENZHEN – The billboards along the thoroughfares of this metropolis welcome U.S. President Donald Trump and other world leaders next week with a futuristic pitch: “Gather in Shenzhen, Witness the Wonders.” Driverless taxis nearby weave through traffic while delivery drones fly coffee orders to customers in a park. The Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum taking place on Nov. 18 and 19 is something of a coming-out party for this southern city, which the Chinese Communist Party used as an early test bed for its embrace of business and market economics.",
    body: "SHENZHEN – The billboards along the thoroughfares of this metropolis welcome U.S. President Donald Trump and other world leaders next week with a futuristic pitch: “Gather in Shenzhen, Witness the Wonders.”\n\nDriverless taxis nearby weave through traffic while delivery drones fly coffee orders to customers in a park.\n\nThe Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum taking place on Nov. 18 and 19 is something of a coming-out party for this southern city, which the Chinese Communist Party used as an early test bed for its embrace of business and market economics. Shenzhen is now the country’s Silicon Valley, its skyline crowded with gleaming skyscrapers housing tech giants including Tencent, while neighborhoods like Liuxiandong host companies building portable power stations and exoskeletons.",
