    summary: "Yemen hospital faces shutdown risk due to sege on Taiz A hospital in the Yemeni city of Taiz has sounded the alarm over medicine and fuel shortages, warning that it is facing the risk of a shutdown if access to aid and supplies is not restored. \"For two months we have been calling and appealing to the international community, the humanitarian organisations: save Taiz, save health in Taiz, save the Yemeni-Swedish hospital. There is no fuel. We are at our last breath,\" said the hospital director Sami Al-Sharabi. The Houthis have besieged Taiz for more than a month as they try to break into territory held by the Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces. Since fighting reignited in the summer, nearly 330,000 people have been displaced. \"Save Taiz, save health in Taiz, save the Yemeni-Swedish hospital. There is no fuel. We are at our last breath.\" A hospital in the Yemeni city of Taiz has sounded the alarm over medicine and fuel shortages caused by a siege by the Houthis that has lasted for more than a month. https://t.co/vUoimztr5h — Middle East Eye (@MiddleEastEye) November 15, 2026",
